1
00:00:09,730 --> 00:00:12,530
We will return for your decision
the day after tomorrow.

2
00:00:12,530 --> 00:00:15,280
Will that be all right, Mr. Sebas?

3
00:00:23,410 --> 00:00:24,540
Going out?

4
00:00:24,960 --> 00:00:26,920
--Yeah.
--Do you have any money?

5
00:00:26,920 --> 00:00:29,420
No, but if I need to, I can sell an item--

6
00:00:30,550 --> 00:00:31,800
Take that.

7
00:00:32,670 --> 00:00:35,330
Thanks. I'll take it.

8
00:01:01,580 --> 00:01:03,620
Yo, virgin!

9
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:37,420
It has been too long, Lady Gagaran.

10
00:02:38,340 --> 00:02:40,680
Er, I mean, Miss Gagaran.

11
00:02:40,680 --> 00:02:41,430
Yeah.

12
00:02:41,430 --> 00:02:43,230
And you, too, Lady Evileye.

13
00:02:43,680 --> 00:02:48,560
Long time no see.
What's up, you here to get lucky with me?

14
00:02:48,560 --> 00:02:53,480
No, not that.
Lady Aindra is visiting Princess Renner,

15
00:02:53,480 --> 00:02:55,270
and she asked me to give you a message.

16
00:02:55,270 --> 00:02:57,230
Hmm? Lakyus did?

17
00:02:57,230 --> 00:03:00,280
Yes. She says, "We're going to be
going into action on the double.

18
00:03:00,280 --> 00:03:05,450
I want you to get ready
to go into battle at a moment's notice."

19
00:03:05,450 --> 00:03:09,960
Okay, but you went to a lot
of trouble for such a minor chore.

20
00:03:09,960 --> 00:03:13,960
Not at all. Also, I was fortunate enough

21
00:03:13,960 --> 00:03:17,590
to have Lord Stronoff
train me in swordsmanship.

22
00:03:17,590 --> 00:03:22,470
He complimented me on that
strike from above that you taught me.

23
00:03:22,470 --> 00:03:27,020
Oh, that? No kidding? Nice going!

24
00:03:27,600 --> 00:03:30,480
--Even so...
--I know. I will not become complacent,

25
00:03:30,480 --> 00:03:32,480
and wish to devote myself to further training.

26
00:03:32,480 --> 00:03:36,610
That's good and all, but I figure
that move could be countered.

27
00:03:36,610 --> 00:03:39,360
It's time you came up with
another move you can transition to.

28
00:03:39,360 --> 00:03:42,990
Oh, Lord Stronoff told me the same thing.

29
00:03:42,990 --> 00:03:47,790
I'll bet. Come to think of it, you asked
Evileye for something, too, right?

30
00:03:47,790 --> 00:03:49,340
Magic training, was it?

31
00:03:49,750 --> 00:03:50,250
Yes.

32
00:03:51,250 --> 00:03:54,250
Kid, you don't have the talent.

33
00:03:55,500 --> 00:03:57,110
Direct your efforts elsewhere.

34
00:04:00,300 --> 00:04:02,140
You don't seem convinced.

35
00:04:03,050 --> 00:04:06,550
Those who possess talent
have it from the outset.

36
00:04:06,550 --> 00:04:09,540
Take Gazef Stronoff--he's a good example.

37
00:04:10,020 --> 00:04:13,620
Can you ever catch up
to where he is on effort alone?

38
00:04:15,270 --> 00:04:19,020
I'm not telling you to give up;
just know what you're up against.

39
00:04:22,700 --> 00:04:26,030
Foolishness. Utter foolishness.

40
00:04:26,410 --> 00:04:28,950
Those who chase after an unattainable dream

41
00:04:28,950 --> 00:04:30,740
are certain to ruin themselves.

42
00:04:31,200 --> 00:04:33,040
I am aware of that.

43
00:04:33,040 --> 00:04:34,830
You're the type bound for an early grave.

44
00:04:35,580 --> 00:04:38,380
There are those who will weep for you
when you die, aren't there?

45
00:04:38,380 --> 00:04:40,550
What's this, Evileye?

46
00:04:40,550 --> 00:04:43,090
You've been picking on Climb
because you're worried about him?

47
00:04:43,090 --> 00:04:44,720
Musclehead! Keep your voice down!

48
00:04:44,720 --> 00:04:47,300
Well it's true, isn't it?

49
00:04:48,720 --> 00:04:52,560
First, gain some magic knowledge.
Once you increase your knowledge,

50
00:04:52,560 --> 00:04:55,370
you'll be able to tell what
your magic-using opponents are after.

51
00:04:56,020 --> 00:04:59,020
Then you can take the appropriate actions.

52
00:04:59,020 --> 00:05:00,110
Right.

53
00:05:00,110 --> 00:05:03,990
Climb, don't do anything
to resign your humanity,

54
00:05:03,990 --> 00:05:06,070
just because you want more power.

55
00:05:06,450 --> 00:05:07,030
Huh?

56
00:05:07,450 --> 00:05:13,310
Sure, it's not as though humans
as a species have all that much ability.

57
00:05:13,660 --> 00:05:18,350
In fact, many of the Thirteen Heroes
were species other than human.

58
00:05:18,920 --> 00:05:23,550
Black Knight, the former owner
of the cursed sword Kilineiram,

59
00:05:23,550 --> 00:05:26,720
now wielded by our leader,
had part demonic bloodlines.

60
00:05:26,720 --> 00:05:30,300
Hmm... the cursed sword Kilineiram, huh?

61
00:05:30,930 --> 00:05:34,430
Tell me, is that business about it
having enough black energy

62
00:05:34,430 --> 00:05:38,080
to swallow up a whole nation
when its power is released for real?

63
00:05:38,600 --> 00:05:40,200
Where did you hear that?

64
00:05:41,190 --> 00:05:44,110
Lakyus said it earlier, when she was by herself.

65
00:05:46,280 --> 00:05:48,200
This is the most powerful of dark swords,

66
00:05:48,200 --> 00:05:50,910
created by the concentration
of darkness unbound, all right.

67
00:05:50,910 --> 00:05:53,450
Even with a maiden like me,
in the service of God,

68
00:05:53,450 --> 00:05:57,120
restraining it with all I have,
I still wrestle with it!

69
00:05:57,120 --> 00:05:58,250
Hmm.

70
00:05:58,250 --> 00:06:00,130
Then, another time...

71
00:06:02,170 --> 00:06:05,760
Don't underestimate my dark power,
rooted in blackness!

72
00:06:05,760 --> 00:06:09,640
I will dominate your flesh
and unleash my cursed sword power!

73
00:06:10,510 --> 00:06:13,640
Tonight is the time when your power
is at its greatest, to be sure.

74
00:06:13,640 --> 00:06:17,480
But I will not let you do as you wish,
even if it eats away at my own life!

75
00:06:17,480 --> 00:06:21,150
Ring of the Holy Valkyrie,
grant me your protection!

76
00:06:21,150 --> 00:06:22,650
Hey, Lakyus!

77
00:06:22,650 --> 00:06:23,780
Gah!

78
00:06:24,900 --> 00:06:27,150
I-I'm all right, don't worry!

79
00:06:29,910 --> 00:06:35,160
Hmm, the priestess was embarrassed
to be controlled by a cursed item.

80
00:06:35,160 --> 00:06:39,230
So those pointless armor rings
weren't just for fashion's sake, then?

81
00:06:39,830 --> 00:06:42,630
Princess Renner is in danger.
You two, come with me, right now!

82
00:06:42,630 --> 00:06:43,790
Don't panic!

83
00:06:44,250 --> 00:06:47,130
This isn't something we can do
anything about anytime soon.

84
00:06:47,130 --> 00:06:51,930
Either way, the only thing
that can stop adamantite is adamantite.

85
00:06:51,930 --> 00:06:55,760
Yeah. Hmm? That reminds me of something.

86
00:06:55,760 --> 00:06:58,640
I hear that a third
adamantite class adventurer team

87
00:06:58,640 --> 00:07:00,440
has sprung up in E-Rantel.

88
00:07:00,440 --> 00:07:03,810
What? This is news to me. What's their name?

89
00:07:04,230 --> 00:07:06,150
As I recall, it was Momon.

90
00:07:06,150 --> 00:07:09,400
A warrior known as
the Raven Black Hero is their leader,

91
00:07:09,400 --> 00:07:12,320
and they're a party of two,
along with a magic caster named Nabe.

92
00:07:12,320 --> 00:07:17,540
Huh? Just two of them?
So, what great exploits have they had?

93
00:07:18,080 --> 00:07:20,830
First, they resolved an incident in E-Rantel

94
00:07:20,830 --> 00:07:22,960
where thousands of undead appeared.

95
00:07:22,960 --> 00:07:27,210
Then, they exterminated the
Goblin Tribal Coalition headed northward,

96
00:07:27,210 --> 00:07:30,700
retrieved ultra-rare medicinal herbs
from the Great Forest of Tob,

97
00:07:31,220 --> 00:07:33,300
slayed a gigant basilisk,

98
00:07:33,680 --> 00:07:39,850
as well as defeated a vampire
possessing tremendous power, I hear.

99
00:07:39,850 --> 00:07:43,770
Also, they subjugated the Wise King
of the Forest with their power,

100
00:07:43,770 --> 00:07:46,020
and are keeping him in submission.

101
00:07:46,020 --> 00:07:48,780
That's pretty awesome, isn't it?

102
00:07:48,780 --> 00:07:52,320
You mean, that would be hard,
even for you, Miss Gagaran?

103
00:07:52,780 --> 00:07:55,700
Thousands of undead wouldn't be a problem,

104
00:07:55,700 --> 00:07:59,910
but a gigant basilisk,
with its petrifying gaze and toxic venom?

105
00:08:00,330 --> 00:08:03,330
Without restorative measures,
that would be too much for me.

106
00:08:03,330 --> 00:08:05,890
That is the ultimate foe for a warrior.

107
00:08:06,590 --> 00:08:09,130
I know how strong Blue Rose is.

108
00:08:09,130 --> 00:08:13,050
Miss Gagaran, there is no way you could
be outdone by any newcomers to town!

109
00:08:13,050 --> 00:08:15,720
Whoo! Thanks for the high praise.

110
00:08:15,720 --> 00:08:18,310
--Okay, sleep with me.
--No, I must decline.

111
00:08:18,720 --> 00:08:21,270
See, <i>this</i> is why you're still a virgin!

112
00:08:21,270 --> 00:08:23,890
This idle chit-chat has gone on a bit too long.

113
00:08:23,890 --> 00:08:28,400
We need to go do as Lakyus said
and begin getting ready.

114
00:08:28,400 --> 00:08:29,820
Please do.

115
00:08:29,820 --> 00:08:31,400
--Climb...
--Yes?

116
00:08:31,400 --> 00:08:34,530
That sword on your hip--
that isn't your usual weapon, is it?

117
00:08:34,530 --> 00:08:37,160
No, this is a backup sword.

118
00:08:37,160 --> 00:08:39,450
There's no telling what might happen.

119
00:08:39,450 --> 00:08:41,870
You should always keep a weapon on you.

120
00:08:41,870 --> 00:08:44,540
Also, you have the items I gave you?

121
00:08:44,540 --> 00:08:47,930
Do you mean those bells?
Yes, they are right here.

122
00:08:48,460 --> 00:08:49,170
Good.

123
00:08:49,550 --> 00:08:53,050
Keep three healing potions on you, just in case.

124
00:08:53,050 --> 00:08:54,050
Understood.

125
00:08:54,050 --> 00:08:56,550
You're a bigger mother hen
than I'd have expected.

126
00:08:56,550 --> 00:08:58,300
Stop teasing me.

127
00:09:03,810 --> 00:09:05,810
You punk-ass brat!

128
00:09:05,810 --> 00:09:07,560
You're filthy!

129
00:09:07,560 --> 00:09:09,690
All he did was bump into him.

130
00:09:09,690 --> 00:09:11,190
They're going to kill him like this.

131
00:09:21,740 --> 00:09:23,950
What kind of moves were those?

132
00:09:23,950 --> 00:09:26,000
Hey, old man, what are you trying to pull?

133
00:09:26,000 --> 00:09:28,910
Back off, if you know what's good for you.

134
00:09:29,340 --> 00:09:30,710
Let me through!

135
00:09:32,090 --> 00:09:34,260
Huh? What was that, old man?

136
00:09:34,260 --> 00:09:36,470
I will say it again. Depart from here.

137
00:09:36,470 --> 00:09:38,220
Why, you...!

138
00:09:45,600 --> 00:09:47,780
Shall we keep going?

139
00:09:49,270 --> 00:09:51,360
W-We're sorry!

140
00:09:52,820 --> 00:09:53,650
Hey there!

141
00:09:54,360 --> 00:09:58,680
Are you okay? Shake it off.
You have no broken bones.

142
00:09:59,110 --> 00:10:00,490
I'm going to give you some medicine now.

143
00:10:02,280 --> 00:10:03,780
Here, can you swallow this?

144
00:10:04,870 --> 00:10:08,750
That's it. Nice and slow. Good.

145
00:10:09,460 --> 00:10:11,390
There's nothing to worry about now.

146
00:10:13,420 --> 00:10:14,190
Excuse me...

147
00:10:28,810 --> 00:10:29,960
Excuse me!

148
00:10:31,400 --> 00:10:33,400
Is there something you need?

149
00:10:36,740 --> 00:10:38,900
Who exactly are you?

150
00:10:39,240 --> 00:10:43,160
My name is Climb,
and I am one of this land's soldiers.

151
00:10:43,160 --> 00:10:47,780
Thank you for doing what ordinarily
would have been my job.

152
00:10:48,960 --> 00:10:52,330
It was no bother. Now, I must be going.

153
00:10:52,330 --> 00:10:53,540
Please wait!

154
00:10:53,540 --> 00:10:57,920
If you would not mind, could you
teach me that move you did back there?

155
00:10:58,760 --> 00:11:00,800
How do you mean?

156
00:11:00,800 --> 00:11:05,140
I am trying to improve myself,
so that I can become stronger.

157
00:11:05,140 --> 00:11:06,810
After seeing your outstanding moves,

158
00:11:06,810 --> 00:11:10,810
I was hoping that you might
teach me even a little of your technique.

159
00:11:12,860 --> 00:11:16,530
Hmm, all right, please show me your hands.

160
00:11:16,530 --> 00:11:17,390
Sure.

161
00:11:21,200 --> 00:11:24,990
Thick and firm. Good hands for a warrior.

162
00:11:25,410 --> 00:11:29,000
Oh, no, I am no more than a negligible warrior.

163
00:11:29,460 --> 00:11:32,500
I do not think you need to be modest.

164
00:11:32,500 --> 00:11:35,210
Now, may I see your sword?

165
00:11:35,210 --> 00:11:36,130
Right.

166
00:11:38,510 --> 00:11:41,260
Hmm, is this your backup weapon?

167
00:11:41,260 --> 00:11:42,760
How did you know that?

168
00:11:42,760 --> 00:11:45,260
It has a number of dings in it.

169
00:11:45,260 --> 00:11:48,970
I am embarrassed that you had to see that.

170
00:11:48,970 --> 00:11:52,520
I see. I now have a rudimentary
grasp of your personality.

171
00:11:52,850 --> 00:11:57,020
The hands and weapon are a mirror
which reflects who a warrior is.

172
00:11:57,020 --> 00:12:00,530
You present an extremely favorable impression.

173
00:12:01,030 --> 00:12:03,110
Now, please allow me to ask you a question.

174
00:12:03,110 --> 00:12:06,450
Why do you want to become stronger?

175
00:12:06,450 --> 00:12:07,280
Huh?

176
00:12:07,280 --> 00:12:10,910
A moment ago,
you said you wanted me to train you.

177
00:12:10,910 --> 00:12:14,750
While I credit you as being trustworthy,

178
00:12:14,750 --> 00:12:17,290
I would like to know
the reason why you seek more power.

179
00:12:18,340 --> 00:12:20,050
Well...

180
00:12:35,690 --> 00:12:37,360
Because I am a man.

181
00:12:38,360 --> 00:12:39,390
Ho...

182
00:12:39,860 --> 00:12:43,490
Based on your answer, I have decided
what kind of training to give you.

183
00:12:43,490 --> 00:12:44,660
Thank you very--

184
00:12:45,410 --> 00:12:50,120
However, forgive me for saying so,
but in my view, you have no talent.

185
00:12:50,910 --> 00:12:52,500
Let me be frank.

186
00:12:53,160 --> 00:12:55,620
You might die from this.

187
00:12:57,630 --> 00:13:03,010
It depends upon your heart.
If there is someone precious to you,

188
00:13:03,010 --> 00:13:04,510
you should be fine.

189
00:13:06,930 --> 00:13:09,640
I am ready. Please proceed.

190
00:13:10,060 --> 00:13:12,020
You are confident you will not die, then?

191
00:13:15,980 --> 00:13:17,650
Very well.

192
00:13:17,650 --> 00:13:20,480
All right, I will train you here.

193
00:13:20,480 --> 00:13:22,110
What, right here?

194
00:13:22,110 --> 00:13:24,150
Yes. Please stand ready with your weapon.

195
00:13:24,150 --> 00:13:25,250
Right!

196
00:13:33,200 --> 00:13:39,040
Okay, here we go. Please hold fast to your wits.

197
00:14:00,150 --> 00:14:03,150
Is this the extent of your manhood?

198
00:14:04,440 --> 00:14:07,380
I am still merely getting ready.

199
00:14:09,620 --> 00:14:11,850
Now then, die, if you please!

200
00:14:39,020 --> 00:14:44,360
Congratulations. How does it feel
to overcome the fear of death?

201
00:14:45,650 --> 00:14:49,910
You did well to avoid dying of shock.
That sometimes happens--

202
00:14:50,280 --> 00:14:52,830
A person is prepared to die, and as a result,

203
00:14:52,830 --> 00:14:56,210
they go and abandon their hold on life.

204
00:14:56,870 --> 00:15:03,020
F-Forgive me for asking,
but who are you? What exactly do you...?

205
00:15:03,420 --> 00:15:07,420
I am nothing more than an old man
who simply knows how to handle himself.

206
00:15:07,420 --> 00:15:08,550
For now, anyway.

207
00:15:11,010 --> 00:15:12,760
Now, once again...

208
00:15:12,760 --> 00:15:13,860
Hold on a minute!

209
00:15:16,640 --> 00:15:18,280
An acquaintance of yours?

210
00:15:18,770 --> 00:15:19,560
No.

211
00:15:20,270 --> 00:15:24,060
So then, he is not
an acquaintance of yours, either?

212
00:15:28,740 --> 00:15:33,140
First off, my name is Brain Unglaus.

213
00:15:34,410 --> 00:15:38,950
Please allow me to again apologize
for interrupting you two.

214
00:15:38,950 --> 00:15:41,920
Your name--I recognize it as that of a warrior

215
00:15:41,920 --> 00:15:44,670
who once fought
the royal head warrior toe-to-toe.

216
00:15:44,670 --> 00:15:47,580
So then, what can I do for you?

217
00:15:48,670 --> 00:15:50,470
Wh-What is it?

218
00:15:52,010 --> 00:15:56,470
How... How could you remain standing
with death so close at hand?

219
00:15:57,970 --> 00:16:03,070
I'd like to know. That went beyond
what a normal man could withstand.

220
00:16:03,770 --> 00:16:08,780
That was something not even I--
pardon, someone like me, could bear.

221
00:16:08,780 --> 00:16:12,390
Nonetheless, that wasn't true of you.
You held your own.

222
00:16:12,860 --> 00:16:16,090
How did you do something that great?

223
00:16:16,620 --> 00:16:17,870
I am not sure.

224
00:16:18,200 --> 00:16:22,690
However, it may be because
I was thinking about my mistress.

225
00:16:23,330 --> 00:16:24,330
Mistress?

226
00:16:24,330 --> 00:16:28,170
Yes, I was thinking about
the lady whose service I am in,

227
00:16:28,170 --> 00:16:29,250
and got through it.

228
00:16:29,630 --> 00:16:31,190
That's how...?

229
00:16:31,510 --> 00:16:33,260
Lord Unglaus...

230
00:16:34,340 --> 00:16:38,930
He had enough loyalty
to be able to overcome his fear.

231
00:16:38,930 --> 00:16:41,310
People can muster
an unbelievable amount of power,

232
00:16:41,310 --> 00:16:44,270
if it is for someone who is important to them.

233
00:16:44,770 --> 00:16:48,870
I believe that <i>that</i> is the strength of a person.

234
00:16:49,400 --> 00:16:52,070
If there is something else
that you refuse to concede,

235
00:16:52,070 --> 00:16:56,640
then you can demonstrate a power
beyond what you perceive as yourself.

236
00:16:57,240 --> 00:17:00,080
The only ones I've had, I've already forsaken.

237
00:17:00,080 --> 00:17:01,410
That is all right!

238
00:17:01,410 --> 00:17:04,250
I could do it, and I have no talent.

239
00:17:04,250 --> 00:17:07,170
Knowing you, Lord Unglaus,
you definitely can, too!

240
00:17:08,340 --> 00:17:13,240
You are both kind and strong. Thanks.

241
00:17:13,760 --> 00:17:15,430
I really have been...

242
00:17:16,590 --> 00:17:17,930
Lord Unglaus...

243
00:17:18,510 --> 00:17:20,260
You can drop the "Lord" business.

244
00:17:20,260 --> 00:17:24,180
I'm nobody that a person
such as yourself needs to pay respect to.

245
00:17:24,180 --> 00:17:27,940
Then it would please me
for you to call me Sebas.

246
00:17:27,940 --> 00:17:34,450
Now then, Unglaus, would you and Climb
both mind leaving here at once?

247
00:17:34,450 --> 00:17:37,630
It appears I have some visitors.

248
00:17:42,410 --> 00:17:43,700
Over there, as well.

249
00:17:48,250 --> 00:17:50,290
Who are they?

250
00:17:51,460 --> 00:17:55,800
Those are poisoned.
Climb, watch yourself. They're assassins.

251
00:17:57,930 --> 00:18:02,100
Perhaps I will be in the way,
but I would like to fight, too.

252
00:18:02,100 --> 00:18:04,390
As one who preserves the peace in the capital,

253
00:18:04,390 --> 00:18:06,290
it is only right that I defend its citizens.

254
00:18:06,690 --> 00:18:09,730
In that case, I will help you, too.

255
00:18:09,730 --> 00:18:13,900
Well then, I will take on
those three over there,

256
00:18:13,900 --> 00:18:16,820
so can I ask you two to take on this pair?

257
00:18:16,820 --> 00:18:17,560
--Yes!
--Yes!

258
00:18:18,280 --> 00:18:22,990
Now then, I am afraid that
I will be confronting all of you.

259
00:18:26,370 --> 00:18:29,750
Would you mind not going after
these gentleman on the side?

260
00:18:30,420 --> 00:18:31,790
That was amazing.

261
00:18:31,790 --> 00:18:35,300
Yeah. If anyone claimed Lord Sebas
was the mightiest man in the kingdom,

262
00:18:35,300 --> 00:18:37,130
I'd agree with them.

263
00:18:37,130 --> 00:18:39,260
Even stronger than Lord Stronoff?

264
00:18:39,760 --> 00:18:44,180
We wouldn't stand a chance against him
if we took him on <i>together</i>. Now,

265
00:18:44,180 --> 00:18:46,390
here they come. I'll take the one on the left;

266
00:18:46,390 --> 00:18:48,120
you have the one on the right.

267
00:18:50,150 --> 00:18:50,900
Now then,

268
00:18:51,270 --> 00:18:52,230
I hate to ask,

269
00:18:52,230 --> 00:18:55,610
but would you be the fall guy
who recoups my time spent out of practice?

270
00:18:55,610 --> 00:18:59,110
Oh, so that is what the story is...

271
00:19:01,120 --> 00:19:02,490
You were out of practice.

272
00:19:07,750 --> 00:19:10,250
Then this might be just the thing.

273
00:19:10,920 --> 00:19:14,250
These opponents are perfect
for shaking the rust off.

274
00:19:19,550 --> 00:19:21,890
Don't get in too deep
until you've determined his reach.

275
00:19:21,890 --> 00:19:22,470
Right!

276
00:19:22,470 --> 00:19:25,220
He seems like a fairly benevolent gentleman.

277
00:19:43,030 --> 00:19:48,500
Fright is an important emotion.
However, you cannot be bound by it.

278
00:19:48,500 --> 00:19:52,790
If your physical abilities are not
up to the task, prevail with your heart.

279
00:19:52,790 --> 00:19:57,670
There are times when
the mind outperforms the body.

280
00:19:57,670 --> 00:20:01,130
If by chance, I die here...
please tell Princess Renner...

281
00:20:01,680 --> 00:20:04,720
...please tell Her Highness that I fought well.

282
00:20:07,180 --> 00:20:08,310
Martial Art!

283
00:20:08,720 --> 00:20:09,810
Slash!

284
00:20:17,780 --> 00:20:19,610
Well done.

285
00:20:19,610 --> 00:20:22,530
Nice going, Climb.

286
00:20:26,160 --> 00:20:28,870
Seeing as how they
followed me from the mansion,

287
00:20:28,870 --> 00:20:32,290
I would venture that these are Succulent's men.

288
00:20:36,960 --> 00:20:38,730
What did you do to him?

289
00:20:39,670 --> 00:20:44,200
It is a skill called "Palm of the Puppeteer."
It appears to be working.

290
00:20:45,180 --> 00:20:48,010
Now then, to begin interrogating him.

291
00:20:49,060 --> 00:20:53,480
Eight Fingers is a relatively large
criminal society within the kingdom, right?

292
00:20:53,480 --> 00:20:54,770
Yes it is.

293
00:20:54,770 --> 00:20:57,570
I have heard the name Succulent.

294
00:20:57,940 --> 00:21:01,790
Something about him being one of
the adamantite class Six Arms.

295
00:21:02,570 --> 00:21:06,030
So then, Lord Sebas,
what are you going to do now?

296
00:21:06,530 --> 00:21:08,970
I have made up my mind.
The first thing I will do

297
00:21:08,970 --> 00:21:12,830
is go and bring down the place
that is the source of this trouble.

298
00:21:12,830 --> 00:21:16,040
He says that Succulent will be there, as well.

299
00:21:16,040 --> 00:21:18,920
Best to stamp out any sparks straight away.

300
00:21:18,920 --> 00:21:22,670
Can I ask you two to carry
this bunch to a guardhouse?

301
00:21:22,670 --> 00:21:26,680
Just a moment, please!
Would it be all right if I helped you?

302
00:21:26,680 --> 00:21:28,180
Me, too, please!

303
00:21:28,550 --> 00:21:31,970
While I believe that
Unglaus would fare just fine,

304
00:21:31,970 --> 00:21:34,940
<i>you</i> might find yourself in a bit of peril.

305
00:21:34,940 --> 00:21:37,350
Looking the other way,
just because of the danger,

306
00:21:37,350 --> 00:21:40,940
would prove that I am a man
unfit to serve my mistress.

307
00:21:41,610 --> 00:21:44,090
Then you have made your resolve?

308
00:21:47,740 --> 00:21:51,870
Very well. Then there is
nothing more to be said.

309
00:21:51,870 --> 00:21:54,960
All right, both of you, please assist me.

310
00:21:54,960 --> 00:21:56,960


